    "result": "Excellent! The feature is complete and fully tested. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## \u2705 Feature Implementation: Threshold Gating for `frai eval`\n\n### Core Changes (frai-core)\n\n**`generateReport()` now accepts optional `thresholds` parameter:**\n- Validates each threshold: metric score \u2265 minimum\n- Null scores fail thresholds (metrics without references)\n- Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) to report\n- Works with custom metrics registered via `runEvaluations`\n\n**Markdown reports now include \"## Thresholds\" section:**\n- Shows PASS or FAIL for each threshold\n- Displays metric ID, minimum, and actual score\n\n### CLI Changes (frai-cli)\n\n**New `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option:**\n- Repeatable: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`\n- Validates threshold format and value range (0\u20131)\n- Reports invalid thresholds and lists valid metric IDs\n\n**Exit codes:**\n- **0**: All thresholds pass (or no thresholds specified)\n- **1**: At least one threshold fails\n- **2**: Malformed threshold or unknown metric\n\n### Testing\n\n\u2705 7 new tests covering:\n- Passing thresholds\n- Failing thresholds  \n- Null scores treated as failures\n- Markdown report formatting\n- Custom metrics support\n\n\u2705 Verified CLI behavior:\n- Multiple thresholds work\n- Passing and failing thresholds recorded correctly\n- Invalid thresholds exit with code 2\n- JSON and Markdown reports both show threshold results\n\n### Documentation\n\n- `docs/eval_harness_design.md` \u2013 Threshold feature design\n- `README.md` and `packages/frai-cli/README.md` \u2013 CLI usage examples\n- SDK example showing programmatic threshold usage\n\nThe implementation is backward compatible: without `--threshold` flags, reports work exactly as before.",
